<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-NORDBANKEN H1 PROFIT FALLS 21 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-NORDBANKEN H1 PROFIT FALLS 21 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-controlled Nordbanken posts its results for the six months ending June 30, 1997</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  3,016 vs  3,804</p>
<p> Net interest income		     4,924 vs  5,280</p>
<p> Net commission income		   1,220 vs  1,013</p>
<p> Loan losses				   194 vs    260</p>
<p> Dividends received			  101 vs     75</p>
<p> Net financial items			  35 vs    685</p>
<p> Other operating income		    228 vs    202</p>
<p> Total income				6,508 vs  7,255</p>
<p> Capital adequacy ratio (pct)	   12.4 vs   11.8</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)				12.80 vs   12.80</p>
<p> Net income				  2,339 vs  2,753</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll found the bank was expected to post an operating profit of 3.08 billion crowns for the first half of 1997. Credit losses were expected to be largely unchanged at 254 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
